> One of the things I like most about Japanese is that it is a very
> context-dependent language. The reason for it being so highly contextual is
> because a lot of concepts tend to be horribly long things to say. Lojban has
> this same tendency, especially when seeking precision, and so it behooves us
> to shorten our bridi in the same manner.
>
